{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Your crowned ones</b> — the dagesh in the nun we do not know the reason for; it is from the root נזר. The masters of your crown were as numerous as the locust." "<b>And your guardsmen</b> — like your officers, and the word is fourth without a partner." "<b>Like the swarming of swarmers</b> — like the maker of swarmers. Like קדש קדשים (holy of holies)." "<b>The sun shines</b> — like the heat of the day." "<b>And it wanders</b> — like 'when there are no depths, I was brought forth' — from the doubled forms in the last position." "<b>Its place</b> — the place of one of them, for so is the way of the locust: on a cold day they gather very abundantly and surround the city and encamp on the fences, which are the city walls, and when the heat of the sun is upon them they wander and go — not one of them remains, and its place is not known, as though they never were."], :book :nahum, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "He reads מנזריך as from נזר (crown), taking it to mean those who wear the crown, i.e., nobles or princes.", 1 "'Fourth without a partner' likely means it is the fourth item in a list and lacks a paired parallel member.", 4 "The citation appears to be from Proverbs 8:24; the reference to 'doubled forms' is unclear and the argument is cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nahum -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nachum"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:49.152834304Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}